        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "What about:\n\ncount `0` = :restart\ncount `1` = \"don't restore session, but DO confirm unsaved changes\"\ncount `[2+]` = \"don't restore session, don't confirm unsaved changes\"\n\n- One is at the left end of the keyboard. Easier to remember and easier for mouse users.\n- Saying that `9` does `qall!` necessarily raises the question of what happens at 10+. Using `9` instead of zero also feels arbitrary even if it's correct.\n\nCounterpoint: Accidently hitting `2ZR` would be unfortunate.\nPossible alternative:\n\ncount `0` = :restart\ncount `[1-9]` = \"don't restore session, but DO confirm unsaved changes\"\ncount `[10+]` = \"don't restore session, don't confirm unsaved changes\"\n\nThat way the destructive command requires intention.",
            "created_at": "2026-06-30T16:00:16Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/40497#issuecomment-4845501043",
